{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1df5d36482c628b390891f91bd2c4e42dfacfd1e5b2f3e1cf62d05ae8a7df3e8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The UI is self-rendered via a Direct2D/DirectWrite pipeline with themes, translucent backgrounds, shadows, animations, and dirty-rectangle optimization, on a Win32 window with DWM immersive dark mode and high-DPI support."},{"claim_ids":["clm_36335f66754aa7540421f29eb5f9a920fb55979496c35d3e9503177854992ac9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AI integration is HTTP-based LLM interaction with DeepSeek and Kimi presets, offering code explanation, rewrite, inline suggestions, agent tool-result feedback, and an API configuration panel."},{"claim_ids":["clm_400b79043bcfea23abe44a308a3ebc957910fd32a1a2083d4346b8402ee0a593"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is a Cargo workspace split by responsibility into crates including aether-core (text buffer, lexer, search), aether-render (Direct2D rendering/themes), aether-win32 (native UI layer), aether-lsp, aether-dap, aether-remote, aether-ai, aether-tree-sitter, aether-plugin, aether-shared, and aether-cli."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9e9f67a36b6e3a57a448d175052b56300bef5811d39f79bbd4d5bffe22704637"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README reports a test snapshot (dated 2026-07-06) of 793 passing unit tests, coverage of about 47.8% regions / 43.7% lines, a successful GUI smoke test, ~67MB memory, and a lexer benchmark of roughly 500-650 MiB/s."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2b19b57ba367a9da947395975c931a256bee6881a1685017fa611aa91f89965"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The aether CLI can launch the GUI, open a file path, and navigate to a line:column position such as file.txt:10:5."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a6d18f4ce77c2fa6edf69eb5426a5fe440bf8fc20586030948f1c4233057af85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: a pre-push checklist mandates cargo fmt --check, cargo check -p aether-win32, and cargo test --workspace --lib --no-fail-fast; the README also documents workspace tests run with CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 to avoid an ICE, clippy with -D warnings, a GUI smoke test script, and a coverage script."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d2c46354b04eeaf6b5ee9790071705c34ef7881be0a1311269792fabdd8d7417"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The editor uses a Piece Table text buffer with multi-cursor support, undo/redo history, syntax highlighting, find/replace, and auto-indentation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d40631a4abd79ccd20a4e57fa1415db23824a3cb9f38a55814c4ec5bb84a9f38"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Building requires Windows 10 1809+ (Windows 11 recommended), a Rust stable toolchain pinned via rust-toolchain.toml, Visual Studio 2022 or Windows SDK build tools, and the x86_64-pc-windows-msvc target."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d9479f40a9a351c7e75764f50ed2accd83361ff9eefe7c41f2c0486c05a5967b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per the Chinese feature list, the aether CLI supports --wait and --new-window flags in addition to opening paths and locating line/column positions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e566c9e832b219f65dc74af7cf2cd5281569e30f38e2a488a3b9d42023ad8bd7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product currently targets only Windows 10 1809+ and Windows 11; AGENT_SPEC.md also notes the build environment lacked a Rust toolchain, so code correctness had to be ensured without compile verification."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1df5d36482c628b390891f91bd2c4e42dfacfd1e5b2f3e1cf62d05ae8a7df3e8","clm_36335f66754aa7540421f29eb5f9a920fb55979496c35d3e9503177854992ac9","clm_400b79043bcfea23abe44a308a3ebc957910fd32a1a2083d4346b8402ee0a593","clm_9e9f67a36b6e3a57a448d175052b56300bef5811d39f79bbd4d5bffe22704637","clm_a2b19b57ba367a9da947395975c931a256bee6881a1685017fa611aa91f89965","clm_a6d18f4ce77c2fa6edf69eb5426a5fe440bf8fc20586030948f1c4233057af85","clm_d2c46354b04eeaf6b5ee9790071705c34ef7881be0a1311269792fabdd8d7417","clm_d40631a4abd79ccd20a4e57fa1415db23824a3cb9f38a55814c4ec5bb84a9f38","clm_d9479f40a9a351c7e75764f50ed2accd83361ff9eefe7c4